  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Manchala Giribabu vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 24 October, 2019 Author: Kongara Vijaya Lakshmi Bench: Kongara Vijaya Lakshmi Hon'Ble Smt Justice Kongara Vijaya Lakshmi Criminal Petition No.6381 of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "He relied upon the common order of this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, dated 27.08.2018 . However, in the instant case, the FIR is registered suo moto on the report of the Sub- Inspector of Police, Pattabhipuram Police Station.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore the police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act. So far as the offence under Section 188 of IPC is concerned as per Section 195(1)(a)(i) of Cr.P.C., no Court shall take cognizance of the said offence except on the complaint in writing of that Court or by such Officer of the Court as that Court may authorize in writing in this behalf, or of some other Court to which that Court is subordinate.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore the police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "So far as the offence under Section 188 of IPC is concerned as per Section 195(1)(a)(i) of Cr.P.C., no Court shall take cognizance of the said offence except on the complaint in writing of that Court or by such Officer of the Court as that Court may authorize in writing in this behalf, or of some other Court to which that Court is subordinate."
